<article class="env-lemma" id="00I0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00I0">Lemma <span data-tag="00I0">10.41.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $E \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ be a constructible subset. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $E$ is stable under specialization, then $E$ is closed. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $E$ is stable under generalization, then $E$ is open. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      First proof. The first assertion follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00HY" data-tag="00HY">10.41.5</a> combined with Lemma <a href="/tag/00F8" data-tag="00F8">10.29.4</a>. The second follows because the complement of a constructible set is constructible (see Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/005H" data-tag="005H">5.15.2</a>), the first part of the lemma and Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0062" data-tag="0062">5.19.2</a>. 
    <p>
      Second proof. Since $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is a spectral space by Lemma <a href="/tag/090M" data-tag="090M">10.26.2</a> this is a special case of Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0903" data-tag="0903">5.23.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>